Heeler: make EasyTier's packet proxy outbound-only.

Heeler's node only dials out. Upstream, the TCP, UDP, and ICMP proxy engines
honour the exit-node bit a peer sets on its own packets without checking that
this node enabled exit-node service, and in no-TUN mode the TCP and UDP
engines forward a peer's connection to this node's virtual IP to 127.0.0.1. Either would let any peer
on the network reach the phone's LAN or loopback services.

After this patch an exit-node packet is proxied only when this node set
enable_exit_node (Heeler never does), and the no-TUN virtual-IP-to-loopback
forwarding is gone; a ping of the node's own virtual IP is still answered
locally. Subnet proxying through this node's own proxy_networks is
unchanged (Heeler configures none).

The CEasyTier build does not start the packet proxy at all (EasyTier starts it
only with its KCP or QUIC proxy compiled in), so this is defence in depth;
`cargo run --release --features packet-proxy --example security` turns the
proxy on and shows the patch closing both paths.

Applies to EasyTier commit 728ba94b5029240add6204eed591f22e4e039e6b with
`patch -p1 --fuzz=0`.

--- a/easytier-core/src/gateway/proxy/tcp_proxy_engine.rs
+++ b/easytier-core/src/gateway/proxy/tcp_proxy_engine.rs
@@ -553,8 +553,11 @@
                 if let Some(real_ip) = self.cidr_table.lookup_v4(origin_ip) {
                     return Some(real_ip);
                 }
-                let no_tun_local_virtual_ip = ctx.no_tun && Some(origin_ip) == ctx.virtual_ipv4;
-                (is_exit_node || no_tun_local_virtual_ip).then_some(origin_ip)
+                // Heeler: a packet's exit-node bit is set by its sender, so it
+                // only counts when this node itself enabled exit-node service,
+                // and peers never reach this node's loopback through its
+                // virtual IP in no-TUN mode. The node only dials out.
+                (is_exit_node && ctx.enable_exit_node).then_some(origin_ip)
             }
             TcpProxyMode::KcpSrc | TcpProxyMode::QuicSrc => Some(origin_ip),
         }
--- a/easytier-core/src/gateway/proxy/udp_proxy_engine.rs
+++ b/easytier-core/src/gateway/proxy/udp_proxy_engine.rs
@@ -219,11 +219,11 @@
 
         let origin_dst_ip = ipv4.dst_addr();
         let mut real_dst_ip = origin_dst_ip;
-        let no_tun_local_virtual_ip =
-            ctx.no_tun && Some(origin_dst_ip) == ctx.virtual_ipv4.as_ref().copied();
+        // Heeler: exit-node forwarding needs this node's own consent, and
+        // no-TUN virtual-IP-to-loopback forwarding is off (outbound only).
         if let Some(mapped_real_ip) = self.cidr_table.lookup_v4(origin_dst_ip) {
             real_dst_ip = mapped_real_ip;
-        } else if !is_exit_node && !no_tun_local_virtual_ip {
+        } else if !(is_exit_node && ctx.enable_exit_node) {
             return UdpProxyAction::Pass;
         }
 
--- a/easytier-core/src/gateway/proxy/icmp_proxy_engine.rs
+++ b/easytier-core/src/gateway/proxy/icmp_proxy_engine.rs
@@ -92,7 +92,12 @@
         let mapped_destination = ipv4.dst_addr();
         let real_destination = self.cidr_table.lookup_v4(mapped_destination);
         let is_local_no_tun = context.no_tun && mapped_destination == virtual_ipv4;
-        if real_destination.is_none() && !header.is_exit_node() && !is_local_no_tun {
+        // Heeler: exit-node forwarding needs this node's own consent. A ping
+        // of this node's own virtual IP is still answered locally.
+        if real_destination.is_none()
+            && !(header.is_exit_node() && context.enable_exit_node)
+            && !is_local_no_tun
+        {
             return IcmpProxyAction::Pass;
         }
 
